A shift that is zero but for rounding is still removed when astSimplify merges WinMaps and ShiftMaps, or moves one past a MatrixMap, so that a series of Mappings that undo each other simplifies to a UnitMap, and the result does not depend on whether the compiler uses fused multiply-add instructions. The shift is now compared with the rounding error of the values that were added together to form it, rather than with 1e-12. The difference between two large shifts that are nearly equal and opposite, such as two Julian Dates a fraction of a millisecond apart, is kept if it is four or more units in the last place of the shifts.
